// The workspace the Aletheia Go modules are developed in.
//
// The loader that reads spreadsheets is a module of its own, ./excel, so that
// excelize and what it brings with it are optional to a consumer who wants the
// core binding alone. The command line, ./cmd/aletheia, is a module of its own
// for the same reason: its template command writes through the loader.
//
// The replaces below are what let a change to one module reach the modules
// that require it without a release. The use directive alone does not: it
// registers the module for the workspace and leaves version resolution to the
// require, which names a version no tag in this tree carries, so Go would go
// looking for it on the network. Each replace is written here rather than in
// the requiring module's own file because a relative path written there would
// travel with the module. Each names the same version the requires do, a
// version-specific replace matching nothing when the two drift apart.
//
// This file is not part of the bundle a release builds, which carries the core
// module's files alone, and a consumer of any module never sees it.
go 1.24.0

toolchain go1.24.6

use (
	.
	./cmd/aletheia
	./excel
)

replace github.com/Jaetan/aletheia/go/v5 v5.0.0 => ./

replace github.com/Jaetan/aletheia/go/excel v0.0.0 => ./excel
